# Build context for the TEST image only.
#
# BuildKit gives a Dockerfile its own ignore file when one is named after it,
# so the production `.dockerignore` stays exactly as strict as it is. Running
# the suite needs tests, fixtures and the dashboard; shipping the API does not,
# and those two contexts should not be forced to agree.
#
# Still deny-by-default, and the credential exclusions below are not relaxed.
*

!src/
!tests/
!dashboard/
!scripts/
!data/
# The dashboard hardening config. A security test asserts its contents, so
# leaving it out of the context makes that test fail for the wrong reason.
!.streamlit/
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# Caches and build noise, which would bloat the context and can hold stale
# bytecode that shadows the source being tested.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Never, under any circumstance. Named explicitly even though `*` already
# covers them: this file is read by someone deciding whether a secret can reach
# the daemon, and "implied by a wildcard" is not the answer that deserves.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
**/secrets/
.git/
.venv/
